WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
Hi guys! How's it going? Uh - it's very late at night which means that I'm a little bit

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:08.880
loopy and very tired. But that's okay, I had some stuff in the morning that I needed to take care of.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:13.060
Uh - so I'm recording this, uh, in the evening prior so that it will be ready for you guys

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:16.880
and not late which is something that I've been doing a lot. Not entirely my fault.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:20.580
Youtube has been really messing up on its processing. Things have been taking

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:25.100
like three or four times as long as they usually do. Uh, but thank you again guys for your patience.

00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:29.640
Um, also, I'm going to be going to Comic-Con this week so I will have

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.460
videos ready for that and they should all be scheduled, which means that

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.560
they'll be more regular than they ever have been because I made them way in advance.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:40.260
But, uh, other than that, uh, this past weekend has been interesting because,

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:45.180
it's been very self-reflective which is a thing that I do a lot. Um, but, but in this

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:50.340
particular case it's been about, you know, my past beyond YouTube. And I often talk

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:55.980
about what I think about on Youtube and for what I've done on Youtube. Um... but since

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:00.220
I played That Dragon, Cancer, you know I've been thinking about, you know, my, my

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:05.060
younger days, back when I still had the *laughs* vibrancy of youth coursing through my veins.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.820
Uh, but I've been thinking about my
dad, and you know, my childhood and, and,

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:13.980
and, and me growing up. And, and also thinking back on old videos that I've done of course,

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:17.560
Um, but, but in this certain, certain circumstance the one thing that

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:24.360
stood out that I wanted to talk about in this vlog was um... the concept of believing in yourself.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.220
A-and it's a, it's a subject that I've talked about a lot, and it's

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.900
something that I reinforce um... but those are just words.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:34.979
You know, believe in yourself, those are words. It's not an instruction manual on

00:01:34.979 --> 00:01:39.150
how to be better in your life. And not
that I'm qualified to tell you guys how

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:43.950
to do, that but I am qualified to tell you guys how I've lived my life.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.600
And how that's worked for me, um...

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.479
A-and one of the most important things is, something that I constantly need to

00:01:49.479 --> 00:01:57.159
remind myself of, is that... I don't have
anything to prove to anyone.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:01.119
And that may seem like a bold claim, because I do have a lot of expectations to meet. Both with

00:02:01.119 --> 00:02:05.860
you guys and myself, but one of the
things that always keeps me grounded is

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:13.180
realizing that I don't owe anybody anything. Simply existing doesn't mean

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:18.850
that you have a debt that you need to pay to the universe to exist.

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:24.440
You exist, whether or not you think and let yourself be stressed out by those ideas

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.580
and this is a very grandiose topic but
trust me I'm gonna bring it down into

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:34.780
something cohesive that can be understood. But this whole concept of not... owing anyone anything

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:39.070
may seem, sensible at its face, but
something- it's sometimes it's very hard

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:44.210
to get through in your day-to-day life. Because especially in the age of the Internet

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:48.250
you're constantly comparing yourself to other people. And you're constantly

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:52.690
comparing yourself to other, like, people in your field of study that may be

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:56.079
better than you are at what you're doing. They may be a better artist, better

00:02:56.079 --> 00:02:59.699
musicians, uh, better you know, YouTubers!

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:02.760
It doesn't matter what subject it is. I- like, you'll often find yourself

00:03:02.769 --> 00:03:09.280
comparing yourself - to others, and you'll sometimes feel like you owe it to

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:12.340
yourself to be that good.

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:16.299
And that is a horrible way of thinking because, that may motivate you in the

00:03:16.299 --> 00:03:19.859
short term and you'll be able to like get a lot of "Fuck you!" energy is what I call it.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:25.180
Um, but in all honesty, that isn't what really is going to make you go the

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:31.380
farthest because when you are constantly trying to meet the expectations of someone else?

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:35.980
You're letting yourself down. A-and one of the things that's been hard for me to

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:41.880
understand in my life is this concept that I don't need to focus on anyone else.

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:46.510
I don't need to compare myself to anyone, except myself.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:51.920
That's why I look back on my life so much, because I'm not comparing myself to other YouTubers,

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:56.820
I'm not comparing myself to other artists or voice over artists or actors. If I wanted to do that thing.

00:03:56.820 --> 00:04:02.180
I'm not comparing to other people, I'm comparing to my past self and

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:07.950
this may be yesterday, it may be years ago, it may be like my childhood self.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:14.260
Those are the only people in my life
that I need to compare myself to.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:19.460
And hopefully as I go through my life, I'm constantly getting better.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:25.860
I can look back on my past self and I can be proud of what I've accomplished in the past, for when it was.

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:30.000
So you know where you've come from, and you know where you're going.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:33.300
Because hopefully, you've got a goal in mind and

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:36.810
I actually talked about this in a video called "believe in yourself" where I

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:42.060
believe I was riding a bike and talking about this. But I meant it then and I mean it now.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:48.380
You have a goal in mind - and this is a goal that just drives you forward.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:52.220
It's what you burn for in the middle of the night. It's what you lose sleep for!

00:04:52.229 --> 00:04:54.900
It is everything that consumes your life!

00:04:54.900 --> 00:05:02.160
This goal is what you want more than anything in the world and it's right there waiting for you to take it!

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.240
And it's literally right there!

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:08.320
It is what you want more than anything in the world and that's what happened to me

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:16.560
once I found YouTube. I wanted to be a YouTuber SO badly. And I knew there were dozens,

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:21.389
hundreds of other people trying to make Youtube happen. And I- if I had compared

00:05:21.389 --> 00:05:25.589
myself to them, and held myself to
their standard from the get-go,

00:05:25.589 --> 00:05:30.740
I would never have been anywhere! I would have been wallowing in self-doubt and

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:36.890
self-pity at how, "Oh! I don't have as many subscribers as them! I'll never get there!"

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:47.070
I set out ONLY to do the best that I could. I could not live if I held myself to their standards

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.420
and waited for their approval.

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:57.440
I had to approve myself and I had held myself to my own standards - and my standards are really high!

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:02.580
My, my standards may not seem high *laughs* when I'm being asinine and childish in front of the camera.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:07.340
But my standards for what I do, in my life, are high.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:13.420
Because - I've been increasing them every year that I've been alive.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:17.380
I expect more out of myself. I expect better out of myself.

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:23.400
I expect better out of myself every day. And that all comes from the fact that I

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:30.139
BELIEVE in what I do. And that's not to
say I ignore outside opinions I don't

00:06:30.139 --> 00:06:34.970
even ignore, like, people that lash out at me for what I've done in the past.

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:40.350
I don't ignore that! I take that in and I address that for what it is,

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:49.060
and I, I influence and shape my life around it. But at the end of the day I make things that I'm proud of.

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:51.980
I make things that make me laugh.

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:56.080
I make things that make me smile. And it's kind of a selfish way of thinking,

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:00.860
but- and even though I would- like suggest you guys to be selfless and help

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:05.980
those around you - at the end of the day you are you. And you have you to take care of!

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:08.940
And a lot of you guys out there don't take care of yourself!

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:15.780
You give yourself to others, and you give yourself to others. And, and some of you may do it selflessly

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:18.160
and not expect anything back - some of you may expect something back.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:21.900
But you give out more than you give to yourself.

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:25.280
*intense whisper* And you gotta believe in yourself.

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:30.160
You gotta be good to yourself. You gotta be good to the person that you are.

00:07:30.169 --> 00:07:34.820
'Cause you're all you got. Till the end of your days. Friends may come and go, you

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:39.750
you may have lifelong partners, but you'll always have yourself.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:46.930
And you have to be happy with what you got. And if you're not happy you gotta make that goal.

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:52.180
You gotta make that goal, and you gotta make it happen no matter what.

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:56.910
I'm glad we're out of the *laughs* cliché part where it's just "Do it!" and all that stuff.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:08:01.440
But I mean is so much. I've said it before, I'll say it a million times:

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:06.900
I believe in you guys. I'm a walking
testament to the fact that you can

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:10.500
literally do anything that you want!

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.760
But you gotta believe in yourself.

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:22.200
So that is the point that I wanted to make. Tonight in, in this vlog more than anything.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:25.700
Because it's been on my mind this whole weekend and I-I use these

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:30.560
vlogs as just a way to say whatever the hell's on my mind. And take it for what you will,

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:32.760
but I hope it helps some of you out there,

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:40.100
Just know, that I believe in you. If you
don't believe in yourself yet, I do.

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:46.250
So, thank you everybody so much for watching. Thank you for sticking with my crazy ramblings.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:52.600
And as always I will see you
in the next video. Bye-bye!

